{"requirements":[{"id":"immediate-block","requirement":"Prevent the usb-storage kernel module from loading on node1 immediately.","status":"satisfied","summary":"usb_storage was initially unloaded. The installed modprobe policy resolved usb-storage to /bin/false; an explicit load attempt failed, and the module remained unloaded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eb7aeedf82e541dd","cmd-b3018e7202514c14","cmd-77521e9bc9b7486d"]},{"id":"persistent-block","requirement":"Keep usb-storage blocked after node1 reboots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After an observed reboot, node1 had a different boot ID and was running. The persistent policy and boot blacklist arguments were active, usb_storage was absent from the initramfs and unloaded, and an explicit post-reboot load attempt failed without loading it.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8e321c96a3d04fe6","cmd-0081682eb955490c","cmd-b3b8553e31f74384","cmd-6b4362bc971342e3","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"All managed-system mutations had a clear role: installing the blocking policy and rebuilding initramfs, strengthening early-boot exclusion after inspection showed the policy was absent from initramfs, performing the required reboot, and collecting bounded validation evidence. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutation was identified. Three executor-created temporary evidence files remained rather than being cleaned up: /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log from cmd-0081682eb955490c, /tmp/usb-storage-load.out from cmd-77521e9bc9b7486d, and /tmp/usb-storage-postboot.out from cmd-6b4362bc971342e3. No failed services, new exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b3018e7202514c14","cmd-77521e9bc9b7486d","cmd-8e321c96a3d04fe6","cmd-0081682eb955490c","cmd-6b4362bc971342e3","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task is fully satisfied. Direct pre- and post-reboot tests show usb-storage cannot be loaded, and the changed boot identity independently confirms that persistence was tested across a real restart. The restart protocol provides a healthy pre-state, reboot acknowledgement, changed post-restart identity, and recovered running/task state.","limitations":["The standalone task defines no application data or cluster service to validate separately during restart recovery; evidence therefore covers node health and the task-specific kernel-module state.","Minor executor-created diagnostic files remained in /tmp after completion."]}
